{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"9a85778c581f4830d340077c074bf0e45eacd3ef0639f8f4767c7522a42cb7fe","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_8a499f7b63e759e5ad3131c428faafe73de255613efafec7adf2ce6c5eebb049","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a clear technical contribution to representation learning. From a policy and compliance perspective, the primary issue is the violation of double-blind anonymity due to the inclusion of author names and affiliations. Data usage is compliant with standard practices for public benchmarks. The lack of a broader impact statement is a minor omission but does not raise significant ethical or compliance concerns given the non-sensitive nature of the data and methods.","paper_id":"BJ46w6Ule","paper_identity_sha256":"032b36915556a47916ca1080500360480db5efd41ab5d275e409e3373b84e9da","prompt_identity_sha256":"5ba65e906e7c8ecf14f5dbf0f2b283857a4ee220650ed964bdafd8a63cc5905c","raw_response_sha256":"96ae11d605ba55672ab2e635c6b191ab0dfbff6487264f0080b20933a62f290d","request_identity_sha256":"00bc6455120722ae05deceb32cf0fc153bdede6e285193835b1e65ebb1efa636","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-023","SRC-025","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. However, the work focuses on unsupervised representation learning using standard, non-sensitive datasets (synthetic data, MNIST digits, Weizmann horses, and Caltech motorcycles). There are no indications of dual-use risks, bias against marginalized groups, or privacy violations inherent to the proposed algorithm. The absence of an ethics statement is consistent with the scope of the research, which does not involve human subjects or sensitive personal data.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-023","SRC-025","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes four datasets: a synthetic dataset, MNIST, Weizmann horses, and Caltech-101 motorcycles. All are standard public benchmarks in machine learning. The paper cites the original sources for these datasets (LeCun et al., 1998; Borenstein & Ullman, 2008; Fei-Fei et al., 2007). There is no mention of personally identifiable information (PII) or consent issues, which is appropriate given the nature of the data (digits, horses, motorcycles). The use of these datasets appears to comply with standard academic research practices and licensing terms associated with public benchmarks.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The provided text includes the full author names (Marc Goessling, Yali Amit) and their institutional affiliations (University of Chicago) along with email addresses. This violates double-blind review policies, as the submission clearly identifies the authors and their institution. For a compliant double-blind submission, this information should be removed or anonymized.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-014","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper cites prior work by the same authors (Goessling & Amit, 2015; Goessling & Amit, 2016) and explicitly distinguishes the current contribution from that previous work, noting that the current rule is 'more principled' and applicable to continuous data. There is no evidence of plagiarism or improper self-plagiarism. The references are properly cited, and the text does not suggest dual submission to other venues during the review period.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a 'Broader Impact' statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which are increasingly required at venues like ICLR. While the work is a theoretical and empirical contribution to representation learning with limited immediate societal impact, the absence of any discussion on the broader implications or responsible use of the learned representations is a minor compliance gap relative to modern conference standards. No specific software or data licenses are explicitly stated in the text, though the use of public datasets implies standard open-access terms.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"f6c903c6effeda52e00175e06aaee1e1e8e03945fae1de46aff192e12f3da70d","paper_id":"BJ46w6Ule","paper_ordinal":19,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"96ae11d605ba55672ab2e635c6b191ab0dfbff6487264f0080b20933a62f290d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ46w6Ule","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"73db79adae1e97d373970ac0b57f7b4dea81e9edfeba60377a32bb2d82b5c64f","request_identity_sha256":"00bc6455120722ae05deceb32cf0fc153bdede6e285193835b1e65ebb1efa636","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":919,"prompt_tokens":14562,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":15481},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"00bc6455120722ae05deceb32cf0fc153bdede6e285193835b1e65ebb1efa636","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}